MID_EV12_060_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_060_m01_001: I apologize for calling you here once more. I feel that\ncongratulations are due to you again. Well done.
MID_EV12_060_m01_002: But I do have some news that will interest you as\nwell. Though it may be disappointing news...
MID_EV12_060_m01_003: Tell me.
MID_EV12_060_m01_004: Your final opponent, Queen Theodora, has\nwithdrawn from the games.
MID_EV12_060_m01_005: And that would secure your victory—by default.
MID_EV12_060_m01_006: <NCA>Welcome it.
MID_EV12_060_m01_007: <NCB>Protest.
MID_EV12_060_m01_008: <ACA>Is that so? Then I will abide by your decision.
MID_EV12_060_m01_009: <ACA>This has become a tournament of exceptions for all\nof us.
MID_EV12_060_m01_010: <ACA>Yet we still staged some magnificent battles. Dagda\nthe Great must surely have stirred in his slumber.
MID_EV12_060_m01_011: <ACB>A pity.
MID_EV12_060_m01_012: <ACB>I know the weight you place on battle. I had\nanticipated this reaction.
MID_EV12_060_m01_013: <ACB>Yet you should be proud of the might you have\nshown. None could gainsay it.
MID_EV12_060_m01_014: <ACB>Your battle with the White-Maned Demon will be\nspoken of for years, if not lifetimes.
MID_EV12_060_m01_032: In recognition, as Divine Sovereign, I bestow\nupon you the esteemed title Flame Lord of Dagda.
MID_EV12_060_m01_031: For your tenacity, you will be known by one and all\nas the Ravishing Shadow.
MID_EV12_060_m01_015: Now we come to the request we spoke about. You\nhave slain Cetus, so you must have a new wish.
MID_EV12_060_m01_016: I've been desperately curious to hear it.
MID_EV12_060_m01_017: My desire is a true duel with the strongest in the\nDagdan Empire—Mars, the Bringer of War.
MID_EV12_060_m01_018: I will not be satisfied with a mere scrap. I ask for a\nduel to the death.
MID_EV12_060_m01_019: Hrm.
MID_EV12_060_m01_020: How dare—the impudence!
MID_EV12_060_m01_021: Hahahaha! I am intrigued!
MID_EV12_060_m01_022: Long have I lived, but this is the first time I have met\na scoundrel like you.
MID_EV12_060_m01_023: You will certainly provide a diversion—but how\nmuch of one? I accept your challenge.
MID_EV12_060_m01_024: Upon my name, Mars, the Bringer of War, let us\nsettle the battle we started, in the arena!
MID_EV12_060_m01_025: Are you sure about this, Mars?
MID_EV12_060_m01_026: I am unconcerned. And unsurprised as well.
MID_EV12_060_m01_027: This is in fact the reason I have joined you\nhere today!
MID_EV12_060_m01_028: Very well. I will approve this exhibition match!
MID_EV12_060_m01_029: We will stage the battle on the anniversary of the\nfounding—the day of the Dagdan Declaration!
MID_EV12_060_m01_030: You have time to prepare, and I suggest you do so.
MID_EV12_106_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_106_m01_001: Challenging a god to a bout? By now, I understand\nyour drive, yet still—how audacious.
MID_EV12_106_m01_002: Dietrich, while I have your attention, would you\nspare a moment for an old tale?
MID_EV12_106_m01_003: Of course.
MID_EV12_106_m01_004: It was we of Agartha who provided Fódlan's heroes\nwith Crest weaponry.
MID_EV12_106_m01_005: In the Great Undoing, the goddess and her kin stole\nthe surface, so we plotted revenge from underground.
MID_EV12_106_m01_006: We found a man and bade him steal the goddess's\nbones, blood, and Crest Stone.
MID_EV12_106_m01_007: In order to understand the power hidden within the\ngoddess and her kin, we began our research.
MID_EV12_106_m01_008: The very structure of the Crest Stones is truly\nshocking. They contain a conduit to hyperspace.
MID_EV12_106_m01_009: A conduit for the transfer of the matter making up\na dragon's body and the energy to animate it.
MID_EV12_106_m01_010: Our analysis was driven by the insights of one\nsagacious researcher. And it led to a critical advance.
MID_EV12_106_m01_011: We were able to create the first, superlatively\npowerful Crest weapon: the Sword of the Creator.
MID_EV12_106_m01_012: We gave the sword, and the blood of the goddess, to\nNemesis. You know of him, I am sure.
MID_EV12_106_m01_013: The King of Liberation, who led the 10 Elites\nof Fódlan.
MID_EV12_106_m01_014: The surface dwellers, robbed of dignity, gobbled up\nthe scraps the gods left them in their mercy.
MID_EV12_106_m01_015: But if we were to give the wretches the power to\ndefy these gods...what then?
MID_EV12_106_m01_016: We soon learned. They took up arms and hunted the\ngods. Relentlessly.
MID_EV12_106_m01_017: Seeing what they did with this power, their euphoria\nin battle...it chilled me to the bone.
MID_EV12_106_m01_018: They were nothing more than beasts, in the end.\nDriven by instinct. Better forgotten.
MID_EV12_106_m01_019: Having witnessed all this, I cannot perceive\nsurface dwellers as human—not like us.
MID_EV12_106_m01_020: I am not bothered by this. You and I are of\ndifferent make, as we both recognize.
MID_EV12_106_m01_021: Only I may define what I am. Not you, and not\nanyone else.
MID_EV12_106_m01_022: Do you hate us? Do you think us wicked, for toying\nwith the fates of your ancestors?
MID_EV12_106_m01_023: Sometimes, I envy them.
MID_EV12_106_m01_024: In this age, one's hand is often stayed. How fortunate\nmy ancestors were to fight the gods.
MID_EV12_106_m01_025: Ngh...
MID_EV12_106_m01_026: Mars is appallingly strong. Even among the gods.
MID_EV12_106_m01_027: What will become of you when you fight him?\nI cannot envision anything but the worst.
MID_EV12_106_m01_028: I must not lose you. I must find a way to ensure that\nI do not.
MID_EV12_061_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_061_m01_001: More flowers! What am I supposed to do with all\nof these? I guess here is good as anywhere.
MID_EV12_061_m01_002: All these flowers are so lovely...and they show just\nhow popular you've become.
MID_EV12_061_m01_003: It seems no one in this city is speaking of anything\nother than the upcoming duel.
MID_EV12_061_m01_004: It's weird, like a fever everybody is catching...
MID_EV12_061_m01_005: The devout are appalled by his recklessness, while\nthe less so praise his temerity.
MID_EV12_061_m01_006: There is no precedent for a contest such as this in all\nof Dagda.
MID_EV12_061_m01_007: It demands attention. All must know the outcome.
MID_EV12_061_m01_008: When all of this is over... What then, Sweetie?
MID_EV12_061_m01_009: Will you go back to Fódlan?
MID_EV12_061_m01_010: <NCA>Affirm.
MID_EV12_061_m01_011: <NCB>Deny.
MID_EV12_061_m01_012: <ACA>Yes. This sojourn into Dagda has gone on too long.
MID_EV12_061_m01_013: <ACA>I should return to Fódlan. And seeing Elfrida again\nwould please me.
MID_EV12_061_m01_014: <ACA>Then take me with you! I want to see what it's like\nwhere you're from.
MID_EV12_061_m01_015: <ACB>Dagda offers much I have yet to see.
MID_EV12_061_m01_016: <ACB>I see no reason to return to Fódlan yet. I find\nit...restrictive.
MID_EV12_061_m01_017: <ACB>Really? Then that's great. I'll stay with you!
MID_EV12_061_m01_018: Very well.
MID_EV12_061_m01_019: Dietrich!
MID_EV12_061_m01_020: Oh?
MID_EV12_061_m01_021: You've got that look in your eye. Don't think strange\nthoughts about sacrificing yourself for a win.
MID_EV12_061_m01_022: Humans were put here to enjoy their lives. You\ncan't spend all your time thinking about death.
MID_EV12_061_m01_023: At this point, I've been with you so long, I think of\nyou as family.
MID_EV12_061_m01_024: Not just you. Esmeralda and Fabio too!
MID_EV12_061_m01_025: Even though we're not bound by blood... Strange,\nisn't it?
MID_EV12_061_m01_026: It's not strange. I think of you like a mother too.
MID_EV12_061_m01_027: But does that make Fabio my dad? Oh, please, no!
MID_EV12_061_m01_028: I would also prefer not to have you as a daughter, I\nassure you.
MID_EV12_061_m01_029: Heh... Hehe.
MID_EV12_061_m01_030: Look at that! He laughed! There we go!
MID_EV12_061_m01_031: Sweetie, you're going to win, alright? And come\nback alive!
MID_EV12_061_m01_032: As she says, winning is our only option.
MID_EV12_061_m01_033: It seems I also must say it... You have a place in this\nworld. With us.
MID_EV12_070_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_070_m01_001: Dietrich! You are no beast! You are human!
MID_EV12_070_m01_002: Hm?!
MID_EV12_070_m01_003: You once blithely told me you are no more than\na beast.
MID_EV12_070_m01_004: At the time, I could not comprehend this. But now\nI understand.
MID_EV12_070_m01_005: I had thought you were merely denigrating yourself.\nBut no. That was a plea from within you.
MID_EV12_070_m01_006: All this time you have feared you are so unlike others\nthat you are not even human—but you wished to be!
MID_EV12_070_m01_007: Ah...
MID_EV12_070_m01_008: My compatriots and I scorned the surface dwellers\nas nothing more than beasts.
MID_EV12_070_m01_009: But the truth was staring me in the face even then.\nYou are no different from us!
MID_EV12_070_m01_010: Yes, you are human. You have always been human!
MID_EV12_070_m01_011: Please, stop! Stop this now and come back to us.\nYou are human, and I love you!
MID_EV12_070_m01_012: That's right! If you don't get right back here, I'll never\nforgive you!
MID_EV12_070_m01_013: You didn't just save my life, you stole my heart! You\ncan't leave me like this!
MID_EV12_070_m01_014: Ngh... Rrrah. Hah!
MID_EV12_070_m01_015: Sweetie, no! You're going to hurt yourself!
MID_EV12_070_m01_016: Rrragh! Aaagh!
MID_EV12_070_m01_017: RRRAAGH!
MID_EV12_070_m01_018: Hrah. Haaah... Haaah... Haaah...
MID_EV12_070_m01_019: He did it! He stopped it!
MID_EV12_070_m01_020: Yes! Yes! Wait, no!
MID_EV12_070_m01_021: You were sidling up to me, weren't you?
MID_EV12_070_m01_022: Oh, come on. If not now, when? Celebrate!
MID_EV12_070_m01_023: Haaah... Haaah... It seems it ends here. I apologize.
MID_EV12_070_m01_024: Our duel, the purest of contests...has come\nto nothing.
MID_EV12_070_m01_025: No. No human has ever come so close to besting me.
MID_EV12_070_m01_026: Not even my son Breza, who was famed as\na champion.
MID_EV12_070_m01_027: As the Bringer of War, I acknowledge\nyour victory!
MID_EV12_070_m01_028: You are the strongest mortal in Dagda!
MID_EV12_062_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_062_m01_001: Dietrich, wait.
MID_EV12_062_m01_002: What is it?
MID_EV12_062_m01_003: I watched your match. You conceded not a step to\nMars. It was well fought.
MID_EV12_062_m01_004: Your blade seems a little changed since the day we\nfirst met.
MID_EV12_062_m01_005: Not Answerer itself. Its wielder.
MID_EV12_062_m01_006: I may be imagining things, but I wonder if the\ndarkness I sensed in you has waned.
MID_EV12_062_m01_007: Could it be that you have found something you wish\nto protect in this land? That's the change I feel.
MID_EV12_062_m01_008: I do not know. But I have found a place that even I\ncan return to.
MID_EV12_062_m01_009: This change is truly welcome. I will let you keep\nthat sword awhile longer.
MID_EV12_062_m01_010: Use it as you see fit. I shall let the church know that\nI will be the one to speak for your actions.
MID_EV12_062_m01_011: But if the sword reaches the end of its power, and\nis of no more use to you...
MID_EV12_062_m01_012: You must return it to Garreg Mach, without fail.\nPromise me this.
MID_EV12_062_m01_013: I promise that I will.
MID_EV12_062_m01_014: Hmph.
MID_EV12_062_m01_015: You sense a change... Do you think that I\nhave weakened?
MID_EV12_062_m01_016: I cannot say. But you are more human.
MID_EV12_062_m01_017: You give a different impression. A better one. I\nwould very much like you to remain this way.
MID_EV12_062_m01_018: The value of a human is not simple to measure, and\ndiffers from person to person.
MID_EV12_062_m01_019: Being strong or weak is not the whole of it. I say\nthere are other ways to measure someone's value.
MID_EV12_062_m01_020: My world had been a simple one. To take the life of\nanother by force, or to lose mine. That was all.
MID_EV12_062_m01_021: On this journey, though, I saw much, and learned a\nlittle of the vastness of this world.
MID_EV12_062_m01_022: If I have changed, then it may well be that I learned\nfrom my companions along the way.
MID_EV12_062_m01_023: Indeed. I think you should journey on with them.
MID_EV12_062_m01_024: You are young. The world is beyond vast—\noverflowing, in fact, and filled with things to learn.
MID_EV12_062_m01_025: Heh. You sound like a teacher.
MID_NR12_00_m01: <SH>
MID_NR12_00_m01_001: The events of that day—already notable for being\nthe date of the empire's founding—would make it an\nhistoric one, long discussed by Dagsion's citizens.
MID_NR12_00_m01_002: People would praise how Mars displayed\nextraordinary power and great judgment, and would\nalso remember Dietrich's fearlessness.
MID_NR12_00_m01_003: And so the Heroic Games drew to a close with\nthe thunderous applause of the crowds for the\ndisplay of bravery all had seen.
MID_NR12_00_m01_004: Still, what the people did not know—at that\nmoment—was that much was soon to stir and\nemerge from the darkness of Dagsion.
MID_NR12_00_m01_005: —Saint Cichol, "Fearsome Warriors,"\nPart 2, Chapter 12